Access to the medical record (HC-REC-03)

Issuer: Poliklinika Karpatia s. r. o. · IČO 35 678 901 · Račianska 71, 831 02 Bratislava

Under §25 of zákon č. 576/2004 Z. z. the patient, their legal representative and a person authorised in writing may inspect the record and obtain an extract or a copy. Requests are fulfilled without undue delay and in any case within 30 days, extendable once by a further 30 days with written notice.
Verify the requester's identity before anything is released; a written authorisation is required for anyone other than the patient.
Copy fees may only cover the actual cost of the copy; an electronic copy is provided where the patient asks for one.
Psychiatric and psychotherapeutic notes are released only where the Act allows, and the treating physician assesses whether disclosure would harm the patient.
The record is kept for 20 years after the patient's death or after the last care episode, as the Act requires, and prescriptions and reports are also available through the national eHealth system.

